Hi Inaki and John - this is a great discussion and I am trying to implement similar behavior in my simulation, using this branching and signaling, but I am still seeing some arrivals being rejected when they try to seize the 2nd resource. I think it is because there are a bunch of arrivals waiting at resource 1 until they get a signal at resource 2 that the queue is open, but only 1 of those can occupy the spot that has just opened. Could that be the problem and if so is there a way to ensure only 1 of the arrivals is able to respond to that signal?

On Tuesday, April 10, 2018 at 3:35:40 PM UTC-4, Iñaki Úcar wrote:
> 2018-04-10 21:04 GMT+02:00 John Redmond <john.re...@gmail.com>:
> > If you are wondering what solution I ended up using, here it is:
> >
> > Within the seize/release block of the first resource, after the resource's
> > timeout I branched off to check the queue length of the next resource in the
> > line, if the queue was maxed out I used a trap/wait/untrap within that
> > branch to wait for a signal that the queue had space available.  The signal
> > was sent after the next resource was released if the current queue count of
> > the resource was less than the total queue size of said resource.
> >
> > I did this in succession down the line for each resource and it seems to be
> > working, my last step is to factor in and test conveyor belt times between
> > resources.
> >
> > Here's the partial code below:
> >
> >   # RESOURCE1
> > ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> >         seize('resource1') %>%
> >           timeout(abs(rnorm(1,run_times['resource1'],.005))) %>%
> >           branch( function() (get_queue_count(fill_line, 'resource2') ==
> > get_queue_size(fill_line, 'resource2'))
> >                 , continue = T
> >                 , trajectory() %>%
> >                     trap('resource2_queue_open') %>%
> >                     wait () %>%
> >                     untrap('resource2_queue_open')) %>%
> >         release('resource1') %>%
> >   # RESOURCE2
> > ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> >         seize('resource2') %>%
> >           timeout(abs(rnorm(1,run_times['resource2'],.005))) %>%
> >           branch( function() (get_queue_count(fill_line, 'resource3') ==
> > get_queue_size(fill_line, 'resource3'))
> >                 , continue = T
> >                 , trajectory() %>%
> >                     trap('resource3_queue_open') %>%
> >                     wait () %>%
> >                     untrap('resource3_queue_open')) %>%
> >         release('resource2') %>%
> >         branch( function() (get_queue_count(fill_line, 'resource2') <
> > get_queue_size(fill_line, 'resource2'))
> >               , continue = T
> >               , trajectory() %>%
> >                 send('resource2_queue_open')) %>%
> >   # RESOURCE3
> > ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> > ...etc...
> >
