> Hi Inaki and John - this is a great discussion and I am trying to implement
> similar behavior in my simulation, using this branching and signaling, but I
> am still seeing some arrivals being rejected when they try to seize the 2nd
> resource. I think it is because there are a bunch of arrivals waiting at
> resource 1 until they get a signal at resource 2 that the queue is open, but
> only 1 of those can occupy the spot that has just opened. Could that be the
> problem and if so is there a way to ensure only 1 of the arrivals is able to
> respond to that signal?

I think there should be a rollback somewhere in John's solution.
Otherwise, as you say, if there is a bunch of arrivals waiting, many
of them will be rejected with the next signal. I believe my solution
in [1] is a little bit more generic and it takes this issue into
account.

[1] https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer.bricks/issues/7

Iñaki

